AB  - Varicose veins are common and have a substantial impact on patients’ quality&#13;\nof life. Multiple good treatment options are currently available. In this thesis&#13;\nwe describe the indications, procedures, safety, efficacy and recurrence&#13;\nprofiles of the most frequently performed treatments for varicose veins.&#13;\nHealth related quality of life questionnaires are important instruments to&#13;\nmeasure impact of disease on patients and can be used to evaluate treatment&#13;\neffects. We translate and validate two questionnaires for Dutch patients with&#13;\nvaricose veins. In our randomized controlled trail we compare effect and&#13;\npatient reported outcomes of endovenous laser ablation, ultrasound guided&#13;\nfoam sclerotherapy and conventional surgery. We also study the effect of&#13;\nsingle phlebectomy on the reflux of the great saphenous veins and we try to&#13;\nidentify objective criteria for choosing the best treatment strategy for each&#13;\nindividual patient.
