AB  - Abstract This chapter provides a summary of a landmark study in vascular surgery that compared the outcomes of mechanochemical endovenous ablation (MOCA) and radiofrequency ablation of primary varicose veins. This randomized controlled trial, the MARADONA trial, demonstrated a higher rate of anatomic failures with MOCA, but similar clinical outcomes were observed at 2 years. This chapter describes the basics of the study, including funding, study location, inclusion and exclusion criteria, how many patients were recruited, study design, follow-up, endpoints, results, and criticism and limitations. The chapter briefly reviews other relevant studies and information, gives a summary, and concludes with a relevant clinical case.
